  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 959 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nOn Tuesday, we start to see a shift in the upper level pattern as \nthe high begins to shift eastward influenced by an upper trough \napproaching the California coast.  By late week, flow aloft is \nexpected to become increasingly southwesterly and supportive of some \nnot-so-straighforward evolution. At least some of the guidance is \nhitting at both increased monsoon flow with the western trough's \ninfluence, but also another tropical wave appears to perhaps \napproach the northern Mexican coastline Wednesday evening before \nbeing shunted our way.  This will be an interesting setup to watch. \nI wouldn't want to get too excited about these prospects just now \nas models struggle with weakly forced systems. It is likely most\nareas will remain dry. However, the chances for rainfall do \nincrease late this week with slightly cooler temperatures (a few \ndegrees) possible.",
